# Testing

Align with `docs/harness-architecture/implementation-plan.md` § Testing strategy and `tech-stack.md`.

## Layout

- Unit tests: same package or `package foo_test` for black-box tests.
- Fixtures: `testdata/fixtures/` (mini repos), `testdata/traces/`, `testdata/provider/` (httptest SSE).
- Integration: build tag `integration`; optional live API in CI with secrets.

## Style

- Table-driven tests when cases multiply; subtests with `t.Run`.
- Compare golden JSONL/traces with `cmp.Diff` or byte equality; update goldens deliberately.
- Failures: include inputs and got/want (`t.Errorf("Parse(%q): got %v, want %v", ...)`).
- Use `t.Parallel()` only when tests don't share mutable global state or temp dirs.

## Fakes

- `internal/provider/replay` for director loop regression.
- `net/http/httptest` for provider adapters — no real network in default `go test`.
- Fake provider for canned tool calls in director/tool runtime unit tests.

## Comments in tests

Same rule as production: no narrating comments. Test names and helpers should explain intent.
